# Scenario 'boot_combos': hidden power-on modes. Every non-empty subset of the 8 buttons (255 combinations, in binary order over
# A B SELECT START RIGHT LEFT UP DOWN) is held for the first 200 frames after a power cycle (`reset`), released, and the ROM runs for 200 more
# frames (title screen), then the next combination follows. Nothing is pressed afterwards, so any code that only runs for a held combination
# (test modes, debug menus) shows up in the coverage. SRAM and adapter configuration are those of the parent scenario; the adapter is present.
# Starts from the state left by 'tutorial_profile'. Deterministic (no randomness).
reset
hold A 200
wait 200
shot combo_1
reset
hold B 200
wait 200
shot combo_2
reset
hold A+B 200
wait 200
reset
hold SELECT 200
wait 200
